Key Idea : Small anion forms stable compounds with small cation.
The thermal stability of alkali metal hydrides decreases as :

\mathrm{LiH}>\mathrm{NaH}>\mathrm{KH}>\mathrm{RbH}>\mathrm{CsH}

because the size of cation increases as :

\mathrm{Li}^{+} < \mathrm{Na}^{+} < \mathrm{K}^{+} < \mathrm{Rb}^{+} < \mathrm{Cs}^{+}

Key Idea : Volume of a gas at $S T P=22.4 \mathrm{~L}\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{C}_3 \mathrm{H}_8+5 \mathrm{O}_2 \longrightarrow 3 \mathrm{CO}_2+4 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O} \\
& 22.4 \mathrm{~L} \quad 5 \times 22.4 \mathrm{~L}
\end{aligned}\because$ To burn $22.4 \mathrm{~L} \mathrm{C}_3 \mathrm{H}_8$ the oxygen required is
$=5 \times 22.4 \mathrm{~L}\therefore$ To burn $1 \mathrm{LC}_3 \mathrm{H}_8$ the oxygen required will be
$\begin{aligned}
& =\frac{5 \times 22.4}{22.4} \\
& =5 \mathrm{~L}
\end{aligned}$

Key Idea :
$\begin{gathered}
K E=\frac{3}{2} R T \\
\mathrm{KE} \propto \mathrm{T}
